# Build context exclusions, shared by docker/Dockerfile.{api,storefront,admin}.
#
# Everything here is either (a) rebuilt inside the image, (b) a secret, or
# (c) irrelevant to a runtime image. Keeping it out matters twice: the context
# tarball is sent to the daemon on every build, and a stale host artefact
# leaking in (a `dist/` built from different source, a `.next/` from a
# different NODE_ENV) is the kind of difference that only shows up in
# production.

# --- Rebuilt inside the image -------------------------------------------------
# Host node_modules are pnpm symlink farms pointing at absolute host paths;
# copying them in produces a tree that resolves to nothing.
node_modules
**/node_modules
# Compiled output. The images run `tsc` / `next build` themselves — a copied
# `dist/` would shadow the fresh one and could predate the source beside it.
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Secrets and local state --------------------------------------------------
# A developer .env would otherwise be baked into the image layer, where it
# survives every later `docker run --env-file` that was meant to replace it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.production.example
.git
.gitignore

# --- Test and CI artefacts ----------------------------------------------------
# Also keeps test sources out of `next build`'s type-check pass, which reads
# the app tsconfig's `include` and would otherwise typecheck Playwright specs
# that import devDependencies the production install does not have.
**/test
**/e2e
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
**/vitest.config.ts
**/playwright.config.ts
.github

# --- Not needed by any image --------------------------------------------------
docs
README.md
.claude
.prettierrc.json
eslint.config.mjs

# --- Docker's own files -------------------------------------------------------
# A change to the compose file or the Caddyfile must not invalidate the build
# cache of three images that never read them.
docker
